    "local_operation": "C_VerifyInit(vendor CKM_KMAC_128 = 0x80000100, CK_PQCTODAY_KMAC_PARAMS{pCustomization = customizationHex bytes, ulCustomizationLen, ulOutputLen = macLen/8}) on the imported key + C_Verify(msg, mac); CKR_OK for testPassed=true, CKR_SIGNATURE_INVALID for testPassed=false. The mechanism is vendor-defined (not PKCS#11 v3.2)",
    "transformation": "subset only; every retained field is byte-copied from the upstream file (hex case preserved); no value is re-derived",
    "subset_policy": "Every byte-aligned (keyLen, msgLen and macLen all multiples of 8) non-XOF case in the pinned KMAC-128 sample: two cases, both in the MVT group with hex customization (one valid, one invalid). Every other group is listed in notExecuted: KMACXOF has no mechanism, and the remaining non-XOF cases use bit-oriented key/message/MAC lengths PKCS#11 cannot express. The KMAC-256 sample has no byte-aligned non-XOF case, so KMAC-256 has no NIST case here (the older kmac_test KMAC256 case stays quarantined).",
    "retained_fields": "tcId, testPassed, key, keyLen, msg, msgLen, mac, macLen, customization, customizationHex",
    "negative_classes_upstream": ["MVT testPassed=false (modified MAC)"]
